{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Know</b> — He alone is Elohim, and we are His people. The word is like every instance of qeri and ketiv. Therefore the Gaon [Saadia] said: כי ולו אנחנו (for we are His) is the opposite of ואני עשיתני, and the word עמו (with Him) in it goes back to דעו (Know)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 100, :notes {0 "The clause 'כי ולו אנחנו הפך ואני עשיתני' is cryptic: Ibn Ezra reports the Gaon's reading without elaboration; rendered hyper-literally without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:37.869546121Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}